\title{nchsNatality: read and losslessly pack NCHS natality public-use files}
\description{
The NCHS natality public-use file is fixed width: one record per birth, no
delimiters and no quoting. That defeats delimiter-sniffing readers such as
\code{\link[data.table:fread]{data.table::fread()}}. This package reads the file by byte position, using a
record layout and value labels extracted from the NCHS User Guide.
}
\details{
Main functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=check_natality_file]{check_natality_file()}} reports line endings and record length.
\item \code{\link[=diagnose_layout]{diagnose_layout()}} checks that the documented layout fits the file.
\item \code{\link[=read_natality]{read_natality()}} reads fields into a \code{data.table}, typed or raw.
\item \code{\link[=label_natality]{label_natality()}} turns categorical codes into labelled factors.
\item \code{\link[=natality_pack]{natality_pack()}} writes compact, sharded Parquet that is checked to be
lossless; \code{\link[=natality_verify]{natality_verify()}} and \code{\link[=natality_unpack]{natality_unpack()}} go with it.
\item \code{\link[=natality_layout]{natality_layout()}} and \code{\link[=natality_values]{natality_values()}} return the layout and the
value labels.
}
